From: MiniHub Contributors
Subject: esp-rainmaker: first boot without a client certificate is not an error

With CONFIG_ESP_RMAKER_SELF_CLAIM=y the certificate is provisioned only after
the node gets IP connectivity and claiming succeeds. Upstream logs this expected
pre-claim state at ERROR level ("Failed to get client cert") on every MQTT
connection attempt. Report it at INFO instead; control flow is unchanged.

Component: espressif/esp-rainmaker v1.16.0 (commit afda50d)
File: components/esp_rainmaker/src/core/esp_rmaker_client_data.c
# Remapped by apply_component_patches.sh onto $MINIHUB_APP_DIR/... when the
# build product is not application/minihub (e.g. minihub_lcd).
Apply-Root: application/minihub/managed_components/espressif__esp_rainmaker

Apply: ./tools/apply_component_patches.sh
---
--- a/src/core/esp_rmaker_client_data.c
+++ b/src/core/esp_rmaker_client_data.c
@@ -217,8 +217,10 @@
     mqtt_conn_params->client_key_len = esp_rmaker_get_client_key_len();
 #endif
 
     if ((mqtt_conn_params->client_cert = esp_rmaker_get_client_cert()) == NULL) {
-        ESP_LOGE(TAG, "Failed to get client cert");
+        /* Self Claim provisions the certificate only after IP connectivity.
+         * A missing certificate on first boot is expected, not an error. */
+        ESP_LOGI(TAG, "Client certificate not provisioned yet; waiting for claim");
         goto init_err;
     }
     mqtt_conn_params->client_cert_len = esp_rmaker_get_client_cert_len();
